you are experinced python developer and your task is to create a gui notes managing app, notes are todo reminders and have completion status

requirements

gui
must be dark, but not black and white (high contrast). use dark blue background and light pastelle colors for foreground
main window is filled with tabbed container
each tab represents thematic group of notes (example: shopping list)
tab can be created, deleted dragged to lefto or right or renamed
when last tab is deleted, automatically create new tab and name it new group
tab has two panes and is divided vertically, left pane is scrollable list of notes represented as cards, right side displays selected note contents
notes pane has filters so displayed motes can be filtered by status
notes pane has additional filter by date and filters can be combined
notes pane has search box so that notes can be filtered by text
serch box has selectable check box 'titles only' that switches search from only in titles or note body included when searching
search is case insensitive
use some basic graphics like characters to diplay checkmarks for done status, X for cancelled and so on

notes
appear as a two text line card, first line shows text from note body, truncated to fit card with, second line shows note creation date, and status as todo, in progress, done, cancelled
each status is color coded and can be changed at any time (even cancelled or done notes can be changed to previous statuses)
notes can be created or deleted

Storage
use json file notes.json to store app data
file is in the same folder as app executable
json architecture: top level is array of objects that represent tabs
every tab object has array of objects that represent individual notes
note object has fields that store note body, creation date, status, ....

Navigation
tab key switches tabs
up/down keys move through note list

Behaviour
when app starts load json data and fill tabs
after user makes changes automatically save json, there is no dedicated save button
changes include tabs (create, delete, rename, reposition); notes (create, delete, change status, type)


